From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:41:45 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: sequencing: pcie-m2: Match WCN7850 with Qualcomm's
 default subsystem ID

Commit a39ac4651e3b ("power: sequencing: pcie-m2: Match WCN6855 and
WCN7851 UART BT variants by subdevice ID") limited the WCN7850 entry to
subsystem 17cb:337c. The WCN7850 in the Microsoft Surface Laptop 8
reports subsystem 17cb:1107, so the driver no longer creates the serdev
and Bluetooth node for it, and its Bluetooth controller is never probed.

Add a match for 17cb:1107. This is Qualcomm's default subsystem ID (the
vendor and device IDs repeated), not an ID assigned by the laptop maker,
so the entry also matches other WCN7850 cards that keep the default. The
driver creates the serdev only when the connector node describes a UART
link for Bluetooth; on such a board, a card that keeps the default ID
but routes Bluetooth over USB would again get a serdev that fails to
probe.

Fixes: a39ac4651e3b ("power: sequencing: pcie-m2: Match WCN6855 and WCN7851 UART BT variants by subdevice ID")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
index e42e85f4762..291c7410e7c 100644
--- a/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
+++ b/drivers/power/sequencing/pwrseq-pcie-m2.c
@@ -199,6 +199,9 @@ static const struct pci_device_id pwrseq_m2_pci_ids[] = {
 	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)"qcom,wcn7850-bt" },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1107, PCI_VENDOR_ID_LENOVO, 0xe0e9),
 	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)"qcom,wcn7850-bt" },
+	/* Qualcomm's default subsystem ID, used by the Surface Laptop 8 */
+	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1107, PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x1107),
+	  .driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t)"qcom,wcn7850-bt" },
 	{ } /* Sentinel */
 };
 
